Hecks.hecksagon "Fibroblast" do
  # Fibroblast wiring. The repair sweep's side effect is no longer an
  # imperative `:exec` adapter resolved by a hand-written Rust arm — it
  # is ordinary bluebook now. See fibroblast.bluebook's
  # `RunSweepOnSweepRan` policy : when Fibroblast.Sweep emits SweepRan,
  # the policy fires the generic process-spawn primitive
  # `Primitive::Process.Spawn` (literal cmd `bash bin/fibroblast_sweep.sh`,
  # result_into `Cascade.RecordResult`). The runtime's one generic
  # primitive hook runs the script and cascades the outcome — the
  # adapters-as-bluebook first slice (plan: structured-pondering-pie).
  #
  # The Fibroblast bluebook (sibling fibroblast.bluebook) names the
  # healing lifecycle (ReceiveSignal, SelectStrategy, Heal, Decline,
  # RecordOutcome) plus the Sweep tick and the repair-arm policy. The
  # script bin/fibroblast_sweep.sh is the impure leaf the primitive
  # runs ; it reads the open queue and dispatches SelectStrategy → Heal
  # (verified) OR Decline per record.
  #
  # SAFETY STANCE (the trust-earning slice) : the sweeper auto-APPLIES
  # only the one mechanical, verifiable strategy — nav_sitemap_close
  # (write missing sitemap entries / prune dead URLs, then re-Check
  # NavSitemapParity and confirm the drift cleared before recording
  # closed). Every ambiguous strategy (bluebook_first_file_gap,
  # loc_ratchet_extract) is DECLINED with a composed proposed-fix for
  # human review — it touches no code. The sweeper never commits ; a
  # human reviews the working-tree change. Over-reaching is the failure
  # mode the fibroblast disciplines against.
  #
  # cwd contract : the process-spawn primitive (exec_dispatcher leaf)
  # inherits the runtime process cwd. The script resolves all state
  # paths from $HECKS_INFO (always set by the runtime) and the
  # aggregates root from its own location, so it works whether a loop
  # member or a manual dispatch fired the sweep.

  adapter :memory
end
